<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Tam Dao by Motorbike: Route Planning | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Tam Dao is the ridge town that hangs in the clouds north of Hanoi&rsquo;s plain, a former French hill station of cool air and fog-wrapped mornings that the city has been escaping to for a century, and riding there by motorbike is one of the most rewarding trips a renter can take. The route&rsquo;s character is decided by its ending, because the day finishes on a mountain climb that forgives nothing skipped in the morning&rsquo;s plan. This guide covers the shape of the ride, the road types, the checks to make before departure, and the discipline that keeps the plan honest.</p>
<p>The machine for the trip can come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk hands bikes to riders heading for the northern hills every week and answers route questions almost daily. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, study the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
